2.2.1

The app version the pictures in this folder show.

One line, in one file, because the README used to carry it in prose beside the version
of every earlier retake -- 1.1.65 split the first launch into three screens, 1.1.67 gave
the app its wallet icon, 1.1.82 redrew the six -- and a reader could not tell which of
those numbers was the answer and which was the history.

check.js reads it. Rewrite it in the same commit that replaces the pictures, never on
its own: the file is a claim about what is in the folder, and a number nobody re-took
anything for is worse than no number.

The app's pictures are the app's own gallery: screens drawn off the JVM by the app's
GalleryTest, rendered from the release tag named above (a worktree of the tag, not the
working tree), in the Yellow accent, scaled from 1078 to 780 wide (780x1736) and saved as
WebP at quality 0.9 (site v2.19.0; PNG before). Scenes: 03-01-Home, 05-Transactions,
07-Accounts-All, 07-Accounts-Tab-Invest, 09-Loans-Given, 06-Analytics, 11-Backups-On,
06-Money-Flow (app-flow-*, since site v2.21.0), and for step 4 01-02-Welcome-Name-Typed,
01-04-Create-PIN, 01-05-Confirm-PIN. Every scene has its own Bangla render (-bn) since site
v2.20.0. The gallery's sample ledger is not the owner's, and it is dated back from the day
of the render -- so a render early in a month shows that month nearly empty.

For site v2.21.0 (rendered 2026-11-03), and again for v2.22.0 (2026-11-05),
v2.23.0 (2026-11-06), v2.23.1 (2026-11-09) and v2.23.2 (2026-11-10), the worktree's
GalleryTest was changed before the render, and the change was not committed to the app: the base sample ledger gained every
kind of entry between the 1st of the render's month and the render (salary, business
income, rent, bills, bazar, food, transport, a transfer, a deposit, a withdrawal), so
Home, Transactions, Analytics, Money Flow and Accounts read a lived-in month; and
06-Money-Flow gained a Bangla scene, which the app's gallery lacks. 06-Analytics and
06-Money-Flow were drawn inside MainScreen (Main(AppPage.STATISTICS / MONEY_FLOW), tests
webAnalytics* and webFlow* in Gallery03HomeTest), because the gallery's own scenes draw
the page alone, with no title bar, and the picture opened on a card cut at the top.
For v2.22.0 also: the site's scenes (the test methods GalleryTest lists as webScene) share
the one base ledger -- Accounts, Transactions and Loans no longer add their own extra
accounts, entries and reversal, so every picture shows the same net worth (Home's ৳3,06,370
on the render day) and no reversal heads Transactions; the FDR, the DPS and the hidden bank
are opened through the journal (postOpeningBalance), not as a balance on the row, which Home
read as Invest ৳0; two more loans given (one part repaid) fill the Loans page; last month
gets entries in the same first days as this one, so Analytics has a "vs" figure; and the
Bangla scenes carry Bangla notes and names (করিম, হাতে নগদ, বাসা ভাড়া).
Until the app's own gallery does all this, do the same again at the next retake.

Since site v2.21.0 the app's pictures have a gap at the top (56px) and the bottom (32px)
in the screen's own colour, where a phone has its status bar and gesture area: the
gallery draws neither, so the page's title sat on the frame's top edge and was clipped by
its rounded corners, and the last row ran into the bottom. The render is scaled to fit
the 1648 between (741 wide), centred, with the sides in the same colour.

No WebP encoder is installed on this machine; the PNGs were scaled and encoded by headless
Chrome's canvas (toDataURL('image/webp', 0.9)), one page per picture.

step1-3 are the phone's own install dialogs, photographed on LB_Clean; they are the same
pictures as before, only re-encoded from PNG to WebP.
